 "transcript": {
  "answer": "I can't give you a direct AUD-to-peso rate. My sources don't include the Argentine peso (ARS). The RBA's exchange rate table lists about 25 currencies, and the peso isn't one of them.\n\n**What I can give you is the US dollar rate:**\n- **A$1 = US$0.6947** on 16 October 2026, the latest RBA figure (4pm AEST).\n- It moved between about US$0.693 and US$0.700 in the first half of October 2026.\n\n**How to work out the peso amount yourself:**\n1. Look up how many pesos one US dollar buys today. You can find this on Google, XE or Banco Nación.\n2. Multiply that number by 0.6947.\n3. For example, if US$1 bought 1,500 pesos, then A$1 would buy about 1,042 pesos (1,500 × 0.6947).\n\n**Which peso rate to use matters in Argentina.** There are often several rates for the peso, such as the official rate and the parallel \"blue\" rate. The difference between them can be large, so pick the one that matches how you'll actually exchange money. For example, card payments by foreigners often use a different rate from the official one.",
